---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Privacy" path="/privacy/">
  <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
  <h1 class="art-title">What this site collects.</h1>
  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      This is a static site with no database and no accounts. It sets no cookies,
      and there is nothing here that could identify you individually.
    </p>

    <h2>Visitor numbers</h2>
    <p>
      We do not follow you between sites, build a profile, or store an identifier on your
      device. We do track traffic to our pages and the sites that linked them here.
    </p>
    <p>
      That exists so it is possible to tell whether anything published here is
      being read at all. It cannot tell anyone who you are, and neither can we.
    </p>

    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>
      Typefaces load from Google Fonts, so Google receives your IP address when a
      page loads. Self-hosting them would remove that, and may happen later.
    </p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>
      Pages are served by Cloudflare, which keeps standard request logs including
      IP addresses, as any web host does.
    </p>

    {SITE.keys.web3forms && (
      <><h2>Contact form</h2>
      <p>Messages sent through the form are delivered by Web3Forms.</p></>
    )}
  </div>
</Base>
